/**
 * Glammzo-web origin for the mobile app.
 *
 * STAGING ONLY — do not point this at production until you intentionally ship.
 * Glammzo-web must run with .env.development / staging Supabase
 * (project host contains `ixsrimysgjizxfdwaxdx`, not the production host).
 *
 * Examples:
 * - iOS Simulator:     http://localhost:4008
 * - Android emulator:  http://10.0.2.2:4008
 * - Physical phone:    http://192.168.x.x:4008  (your Mac LAN IP)
 *
 * Legal pages (Privacy / Terms) open on the public site:
 *   https://glammzo.com/privacy  and  https://glammzo.com/terms
 * Optional override: EXPO_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://glammzo.com
 *
 * Store listing (App Store Connect / Play Console) — use the same URLs:
 *   Privacy policy: https://glammzo.com/privacy
 *   Support email:  hello@glammzo.com
 * Fill `submit.production.ios.ascAppId` in eas.json after creating the ASC app.
 *
 * Push notifications (Android remote push requires Firebase + EAS):
 * 1. Create a Firebase project; add Android app package com.glammzo.mobile
 * 2. Download google-services.json into this repo root (app.config picks it up automatically)
 * 3. Upload FCM V1 service account key in EAS:
 *      eas credentials → Android → Google Service Account → FCM V1
 *    Docs: https://docs.expo.dev/push-notifications/fcm-credentials/
 * 4. Rebuild Android (preview/production) after adding google-services.json
 * 5. Apply Glammzo-web scripts/apply-mobile-push-tokens-migration.sql on the API’s Supabase
 * 6. Ensure EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL hosts POST /api/mobile/push/register (deploy Glammzo-web)
 * 7. Install the new APK, sign in, allow notifications — token registers on login
 * Note: Expo Go on Android cannot receive remote push (SDK 53+)
 *
 * OTP / login (uses Glammzo-web, not CRM):
 *   POST /api/mobile/auth/otp/request  → challengeToken (+ debugOtp when enabled)
 *   POST /api/mobile/auth/otp/verify   → accessToken
 * On Glammzo-web (local / staging), keep the same fixed OTP as web login:
 *   SMS_PROVIDER=mock
 *   SMS_FIXED_OTP=123456
 *   SMS_DEBUG_OTP=true
 * Mobile shows “Dev OTP” whenever the server returns debugOtp (preview/production builds too).
 * Live SMS: Glammzo-web SMS_PROVIDER=msg91 (no SMS_FIXED_OTP / SMS_DEBUG_OTP).
 * Location / Google Places (web BFF — keep using Glammzo Server API Key):
 * Glammzo-web GOOGLE_MAPS_SERVER_API_KEY with Places + Geocoding.
 * Do NOT put the server key in the mobile app.
 *
 * Map view (Maps SDK for iOS / Android) — create NEW keys, do not reuse HTTP-referrer web keys:
 *   EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_IOS_API_KEY=...       (Application restriction: iOS apps → com.glammzo.mobile)
 *   EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_ANDROID_API_KEY=...   (Application restriction: Android apps → com.glammzo.mobile + SHA-1)
 * Or one shared key for both (weaker):
 *   EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=...
 * Enable APIs on those keys: Maps SDK for iOS, Maps SDK for Android.
 * Then: npx expo start -c  (native builds need a rebuild after changing keys)
 */
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4008
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://glammzo.com
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_IOS_API_KEY=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_ANDROID_API_KEY=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
